<Placemark><name>Former Sears — Metrocenter</name><description>Vacant
9803 N Metro Pkwy W, Phoenix, AZ 85051

Two-story Sears box closed 2020; still standing after the rest of Metrocenter Mall was demolished (2025). ~14.5 ac of empty striped parking around it. Owned by the Sears successor company, not part of the mall redevelopment.

https://www.kjzz.org/business/2025-09-25/demo-of-phoenixs-metrocenter-mall-is-finally-done-see-what-the-the-metropolitan-will-look-like</description><styleUrl>#vacant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-112.123144,33.577375,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Former Kmart — 2526 W Northern Ave</name><description>Vacant
2526 W Northern Ave, Phoenix, AZ 85051

Kmart closed 2017; building still vacant with an &#x27;AVAILABLE&#x27; banner on the front. ~8.3 ac lot. County records show the City of Phoenix now owns the parcel.</description><styleUrl>#vacant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-112.114159,33.554224,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Former Fry&#x27;s Electronics — Tempe</name><description>Vacant
2300 W Baseline Rd, Tempe, AZ 85283

149,000 SF big box closed Feb 2021 when Fry&#x27;s Electronics shut down. ~15 ac site west of I-10 by Arizona Mills. A Costco Business Center conversion was proposed in 2022 but stalled. Confirm on arrival.

https://www.abc15.com/news/business/costco-could-be-planning-a-new-business-center-in-east-valley</description><styleUrl>#vacant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-111.972106,33.379268,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Former Sears + auto center — Superstition Springs</name><description>Vacant
6525 E Southern Ave, Mesa, AZ 85206 (south side of the mall)

113,837 SF two-story Sears (closed 2018) plus 17,050 SF former auto center on ~12.7 ac, sold at auction as a redevelopment site. Apartments have been proposed for the land.

https://www.commercialcafe.com/commercial-property/us/az/mesa/redevelopment-opportunity-for-auction-in-mesa/</description><styleUrl>#vacant</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-111.691772,33.389258,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Former Safeway — 32nd St &amp; Thunderbird</name><description>Closed
3131 E Thunderbird Rd, Phoenix, AZ 85032

Safeway closed this store in July 2025. Grocery box on a ~10 ac shopping-center parcel; other tenants in the center may still be open, so expect some traffic.

https://www.abc15.com/news/state/safeway-albertsons-to-close-3-arizona-locations-including-2-in-phoenix</description><styleUrl>#closed</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-112.014533,33.610249,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
